# 1Password secret references for the gateway's XSIAM credentials.
# Copy to .env.op (git ignores it), replace the vault and item names, then run:
#   op run --env-file=.env.op -- poetry run python src/main.py
# op resolves each op://vault/item/field reference when the gateway starts and
# never writes the values to disk. See docs/SECRETS.md.
#
# Item ids are more stable than titles: `op item get "<title>" --format json | jq -r .id`
CORTEX_MCP_PAPI_URL=op://Security Engineering/XSIAM dev tenant Tier1/url
CORTEX_MCP_PAPI_AUTH_HEADER=op://Security Engineering/XSIAM dev tenant Tier1/credential
CORTEX_MCP_PAPI_AUTH_ID=op://Security Engineering/XSIAM dev tenant Tier1/auth_id

# Credential broker profiles resolve the same way; add one line per key named in
# XSIAM_CREDENTIAL_PROFILES.
# XSIAM_T1_KEY=op://Security Engineering/XSIAM dev tenant Tier1/credential
# XSIAM_T1_KEY_ID=op://Security Engineering/XSIAM dev tenant Tier1/auth_id
